  "_id": "6a7f5797757ee51246381c64",
  "lab": "6a7f5796eda1a5feaff0b458",
  "name": "Scrub Typhus IgG and IgM",
  "code": "SCRUB IgM",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>\r\n<div>Scrub Typhus IgM Test Result</div>\r\n</th>\r\n<th>\r\n<div>Interpretation</div>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Reactive</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<div>A Reactive Scrub Typhus IgM test result indicates a recent or active infection with Orientia tsutsugamushi, the bacteria that cause scrub typhus. The presence of IgM antibodies suggests an acute infection that is likely to have occurred within the past few weeks. Confirmation of the diagnosis may require further testing, such as a PCR test or a rise in antibody titers in paired samples. Treatment with appropriate antibiotics should be initiated promptly.</div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<div>Non-reactive</div>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<div>A Non-reactive Scrub Typhus IgM test result means that no detectable IgM antibodies against Orientia tsutsugamushi were found in the blood sample. This result is consistent with either the absence of infection or the early stages of the disease when IgM antibodies have not yet developed. If there is a strong clinical suspicion of scrub typhus, repeat testing or testing for other markers may be recommended.</div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<div>Indeterminate</div>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<div>An indeterminate Scrub Typhus IgM test result means that the test could not provide a clear positive or negative result. This may occur due to various reasons, such as a borderline antibody level. Additional testing and clinical evaluation are necessary to determine the presence of scrub typhus and guide appropriate management.</div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
